---
title: Extraction Cache Data Flow
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User taps article
    participant APS as ArticlePipelineService
    participant Cloud as extract-proxy Lambda
    participant DDB as DynamoDB<br/>extraction-index
    participant S3 as S3 Bucket
    participant SQS as SQS Extraction Queue
    participant ECS as ECS Fargate<br/>Puppeteer
    participant Web as Article Website
    participant NSC as NSCache (L1)
    participant SD as SwiftData (L2)
    participant WK as WKWebView (L3)

    User->>APS: process(item)

    Note over APS: Premium user: check L0 first
    APS->>Cloud: GET /v1/extract/{sha256(url)}
    Cloud->>DDB: lookup urlHash

    alt Cache Hit
        DDB-->>Cloud: s3Key found
        Cloud->>S3: GET ContentNode JSON
        S3-->>Cloud: article content
        Cloud-->>APS: 200 + ExtractedArticle
        Note over APS: ~80ms total
        APS-->>User: display article instantly
    else Cache Miss
        DDB-->>Cloud: not found
        Cloud->>SQS: enqueue URL for extraction
        Cloud-->>APS: 404 (miss)

        Note over APS: Fall through to local cache
        APS->>NSC: check L1
        NSC-->>APS: miss
        APS->>SD: check L2
        SD-->>APS: miss
        APS->>WK: extract via Readability.js
        WK->>Web: load page
        Web-->>WK: HTML + JS rendered
        WK-->>APS: ContentNode[]
        Note over APS: 2-5 seconds
        APS-->>User: display article

        par Server-side extraction (async)
            SQS->>ECS: dequeue URL
            ECS->>Web: Puppeteer loads page
            Web-->>ECS: rendered HTML
            ECS->>ECS: Readability.js extract
            ECS->>S3: store ContentNode JSON
            ECS->>DDB: index urlHash → s3Key
            Note over S3: 72hr TTL
            Note over ECS: Next user gets cache hit
        end
    end
